# Restart drain

**Invariant:** `needed(restart) ⇒ fire(restart)` — busy, in-flight, a peer's stream, a dirty tree, an open
Cowork tab, or "this IDE session" is never a reason to skip, park, or route the force through the operator.
`edit(served_path ∨ env_loaded_by_process) ∧ running(process) ⇒ recycle(process)` same turn; `bind_mount ⇏ live`.
That recycle is **not** a work-complete claim.

```
∀ service ≠ git_integration_worker:  busy defers ⇒ re-fire force=true, announce
service = git_integration_worker:    arm drain (status=deferred, restart_intent_id) — never force, never kill
  live cursor-sdk dispatch ⇒ park, not wait: manage(sync_restart|restart|stop, park_live=true) —
  GIW cancels the bridge run (row terminal cancelled + park_*), drain converges, GIW auto-resumes
  the row as a resume_of child after restart (inherited execution_id/thread). recycle_giw is
  park-first at idle; force only on CANCEL_FAILED / NEST_CHAIN / STATE_ROOT_MISSING.
```

Discriminator: interruption destroy-set. Attach handles reconnect (`mcp`, `cdp_ask`, `stargate`,
`gateway`, …); only GIW holds an in-progress durable write. Recycling `mcp`/`cdp_ask` drops attach,
not the CSE (`chat_url`) or the IDE chat.

## Forbidden / Required

| Forbidden | Required |
|---|---|
| `pkill` / `kill` / `docker stop` for lifecycle | `manage(action="sync_restart"|"restart"|"stop")` — drain-gated chokepoint |
| Poll `wait_healthy` in-window while holding the write lease (never converges) | Arm, **exit**, probe on a later turn; IDE waits in background |
| Claim `live` from a commit, an import, or `status=deferred` | Process start after served-file **and** env mtime, or a live probe of the changed surface |
| Report exact `live@<sha>` when served dirt was loaded | Report `live` + tree state; `live@<sha>` needs path-explicit commit **before** restart |
| Hold graph stamps / todo close for `live@sha` | Close once ACs met and ordinary `live` proven (or `liveness n/a`) |
| Recycle-as-finished while session paths uncommitted | Commit session paths, **then** recycle; quote both payloads |

## Go-live = work-complete finishing (last)

Default (not a strategy choice):

```
land the work → path-explicit commit of session paths → recycle serving processes
```

`work_complete ⇒ commit(path-explicit, session_paths) ≺ recycle(every serving process) ∧ stamp(graph)`.
"Go live / activate / everything live?" are that contract, not a second permission gate.
`live@sha` is already this order. **Recycle-from-dirty-tree is retired as the ordinary-live default.**
Exceptional mid-arc verify (bind-mount / `docker cp`): mark exceptional and commit session paths
**before any done claim** — not a next-turn sequel. `needed(restart)` mid-arc is not finishing.

`work_complete` ∉ L(x) without quoted commit + recycle payloads. Fluency ≠ the act. Trust tool payloads.

"Only create commits when requested" = opportunistic/unrelated commits; **not** a veto of this
contract. The seat commits session paths without asking. Checkpoint commit and `/session-end`
are not work-complete.

Stamp after recycle+proof when the stamp cites that commit. Proof: services ·
`live|live@sha|not_live|drain_pending` · commit SHA · `restart_intent_id` or process start UTC ·
path probe. Satellites: same via their deploy script.
`runbook:restart-drain` · `decision:go-live-proof-loop` · `git-posture`.
